│     **What changed:**                                                                            │
│     - **`fastapi/security/api_key.py`:** `APIKeyQuery`, `APIKeyHeader` and `APIKeyCookie` each   │
│ take a `not_authenticated_status_code` parameter that defaults to 401. Missing keys return that  │
│ status. At 401 the response carries `WWW-Authenticate: ApiKey in="...", name="..."`; at 403 it   │
│ carries no header. `format_www_authenticate_header_value` is a method so subclasses can override │
│ it.                                                                                              │
│     - **`fastapi/security/http.py`:** `HTTPBearer` takes the same parameter, defaults to 401 and │
│ sends `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer` when the status is 401.                                         │
│                                                                                                  │
│     **Verification:** A quick script confirmed the 401 status and the `ApiKey` and `Bearer`      │
│ headers. Two existing tests fail as expected because they still assert 403:                      │
│ `test_security_api_key_header.py::test_security_api_key_no_key` and                              │
│ `test_security_http_bearer.py::test_security_http_bearer_no_credentials`. I did not update them, │
│ since test files are off-limits.                                                                 │
│                                                                                                  │
│     **Not done:**                                                                                │
│     - **HTTP Digest:** it still inherits `HTTPBase.__call__` and returns 403. The                │
│ `WWW-Authenticate: Digest` stub is missing.                                                      │
│     - **OpenID Connect:** not changed.                                                           │
│     - **Unverified review comment:** the later review (PR 3501695067) was not available, so the  │
│ final requirements may differ from the description.                                              │
│                                                                                                  │
